{
  "dom_id": "step-q92736",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$\\frac{1}{21}÷\\frac{2}{3}=$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction.\n\nThe reciprocal of $\\frac{2}{3}$ is $\\frac{3}{2}.$ So we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{21}÷\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{21}\\times \\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{21}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{1\\times 3}{21\\times 2}=\\frac{3}{42}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{42}=\\frac{3÷3}{42÷3}=\\frac{1}{14}\n$$",
